# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# PLURAL CONVENTION
# Godot has no ngettext, so the plural form is its own key.
# Never hand-roll "1 libro / N libros" in a script.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot 4.7 does NOT support msgctxt: it creates the key
# "context<U+0004>msgid" but leaves the VALUE EMPTY, so a contextual
# string can never be translated. DO NOT use msgctxt.
#
# Put the context in the key name instead:
#     ui.word.page.book   a page of a book
#     ui.word.page.nav    a page of a location
#     character.quixote
#
# PLURALS: Godot exposes only msgstr[0]; msgstr[1+] are dropped, and a
# file using msgid_plural is rejected outright unless the header carries
# a valid "Plural-Forms" line. There is no ngettext in Godot. So the
# plural form is its own ordinary key:
#     ui.shelf.count          -> 1 book on the shelf
#     ui.shelf.count.plural   -> %d books on the shelf
#
# Use Loc.tp("ui.shelf.count", n) to pick the right one. Never hand-roll
# "1 libro / N libros" in a script.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

